## 6. Root cause (code, verifiable)

# The 21:07:46 frame is the expected resize-window skip: recordInternal() returns false at
# the "no usable arg11" guard *after* inject::record() has already Reset the command list
# and the allocator. inject::record() returns false on every sub-record failure WITHOUT
# calling Close(). A D3D12 command list left in the recording state keeps its allocator
# busy, so the next frame's allocator->Reset()/list->Reset() fails; inject::record() then
# returns false at its first line forever. That is exactly the observed picture:
#   - no sr::recordInternal logs after the first failure (fails before it is called),
#   - RecordFailed on every interval, surviving world re-entry and Stop/Start,
#   - no device error / crash: the HRESULTs are dropped silently.
# The two earlier single-frame skips were "no pre-HUD boundary" (prepare returns before
# record), which do not reset the list and therefore stayed recoverable.

## 7. Postmortem addendum (written after EXP-0064 was closed fail)

# Code path confirmed in src/neurodragon/probe/VvInject.cpp::record():
#   Reset(allocator, list) -> sub-record -> ... -> SUCCEEDED(list->Close())
# every `if (!sub-record) return false;` skipped the Close. The 21:07:46 frame took the
# `!target || !sr::recordArg10(...)` branch (arg11 not yet resolvable at 2560x1369), so the
# list stayed recording; allocator->Reset() then failed on every following frame at the
# first line of record(), which is why no [vvsr] line appears after 21:07:46.
# Fix under test in the next attempt: close the list at the top of record() (recovery from
# a previous open list) and route every failure/success return through finish(), which
# always Closes and logs a Close failure.
